I counted four instances. I read the reference as a door swing that hangs down from a horizontal line, with a purple leaf line and arc forming a V. I zoomed only on the right-hand part of the drawing (x 800–1000, y 0–300 and y 480–780), where the door swings are. I did not zoom on the left part, which looked like plain grid lines and circle labels.

I counted two downward-opening swings in each of two rows, one near y≈110 and one near y≈563. I left out the swings near y≈250, which open upward. I treated those as mirrored rather than rotated, so that call is uncertain. The right-hand swing in each row is cut off by the edge of the drawing.

